1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,541
Most Lamborghinis are named after fighting bulls.

2
00:00:03,721 --> 00:00:05,044
The Miura, the Espada,

3
00:00:05,044 --> 00:00:05,706
the Diablo.

4
00:00:05,886 --> 00:00:07,430
The Countach is not.

5
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:09,884
Its name is a word of astonishment,

6
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:11,833
and the story of where it came

7
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:13,717
from is only half documented.

8
00:00:13,897 --> 00:00:15,721
And the car that wears it was

9
00:00:15,721 --> 00:00:17,356
designed with a periscope,

10
00:00:17,356 --> 00:00:19,620
because the driver could not see out

11
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:20,375
of the back.

12
00:00:20,555 --> 00:00:22,440
These are two things you may not

13
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,561
know about the Lamborghini Countach.

14
00:00:24,911 --> 00:00:26,732
We will take them one at a

15
00:00:26,732 --> 00:00:27,783
time: the name,

16
00:00:27,783 --> 00:00:29,044
and the periscope.

17
00:00:29,224 --> 00:00:31,328
Along the way we will also look

18
00:00:31,328 --> 00:00:33,569
at what the sources say about the

19
00:00:33,569 --> 00:00:36,285
prototype that was destroyed on purpose,

20
00:00:36,285 --> 00:00:37,507
the scissor doors,

21
00:00:37,507 --> 00:00:38,593
and the numbers.

22
00:00:38,773 --> 00:00:41,615
Every fact comes from a published source,

23
00:00:41,615 --> 00:00:43,417
listed in the description.

24
00:00:43,597 --> 00:00:45,405
Where sources disagree,

25
00:00:45,405 --> 00:00:46,348
we tell you.

26
00:00:46,528 --> 00:00:48,205
Where we do the maths,

27
00:00:48,205 --> 00:00:48,967
we say so.

28
00:00:49,317 --> 00:00:53,159
Ferruccio Lamborghini named his cars after bulls.

29
00:00:53,339 --> 00:00:56,093
Wikipedia says the Miura was named after

30
00:00:56,093 --> 00:00:58,502
a family of Spanish fighting bulls,

31
00:00:58,502 --> 00:01:00,980
and that he visited their ranch near

32
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,045
Seville in nineteen sixty-two.

33
00:01:03,225 --> 00:01:05,293
The list continues:

34
00:01:05,293 --> 00:01:07,796
Islero, Espada, Jarama,

35
00:01:07,796 --> 00:01:10,516
Urraco, Jalpa and Diablo.

36
00:01:10,696 --> 00:01:13,229
The page says the Countach broke that

37
00:01:13,229 --> 00:01:14,667
tradition completely.

38
00:01:15,017 --> 00:01:18,694
The name comes from a Piedmontese exclamation

39
00:01:18,694 --> 00:01:21,309
of astonishment, Wikipedia says.

40
00:01:21,489 --> 00:01:23,532
The page spells it contacc.

41
00:01:23,712 --> 00:01:26,012
The designer, Marcello Gandini,

42
00:01:26,012 --> 00:01:27,421
spells it countach,

43
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:29,794
and says the word was first used

44
00:01:29,794 --> 00:01:31,426
as a joke by a worker,

45
00:01:31,426 --> 00:01:32,687
and then adopted.

46
00:01:32,867 --> 00:01:33,753
He calls it,

47
00:01:33,753 --> 00:01:35,526
in the page's quotation,

48
00:01:35,526 --> 00:01:38,184
the only true story behind the word.

49
00:01:38,364 --> 00:01:40,835
The name was coined in late nineteen

50
00:01:40,835 --> 00:01:43,032
seventy or nineteen seventy-one.

51
00:01:43,381 --> 00:01:45,158
Now the part that is not settled.

52
00:01:45,338 --> 00:01:47,176
Gandini says the word,

53
00:01:47,176 --> 00:01:48,513
as he spells it,

54
00:01:48,513 --> 00:01:51,520
literally means plague or contagion,

55
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:54,278
but is used to express amazement.

56
00:01:54,458 --> 00:01:58,189
The Wikipedia article itself describes it only

57
00:01:58,189 --> 00:02:00,947
as an exclamation of astonishment.

58
00:02:01,127 --> 00:02:04,002
So two descriptions of the same word,

59
00:02:04,002 --> 00:02:05,556
in the same article,

60
00:02:05,556 --> 00:02:07,188
do not match exactly.

61
00:02:07,368 --> 00:02:09,760
We report both rather than choosing.

62
00:02:10,109 --> 00:02:12,636
There is also the popular story that

63
00:02:12,636 --> 00:02:15,863
Nuccio Bertone saw the prototype and exclaimed

64
00:02:15,863 --> 00:02:16,495
the word.

65
00:02:16,675 --> 00:02:19,807
Wikipedia marks that story as needing a

66
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:20,529
citation.

67
00:02:20,709 --> 00:02:21,739
In other words,

68
00:02:21,739 --> 00:02:23,728
the page does not support it.

69
00:02:23,908 --> 00:02:25,717
It is a good story and it

70
00:02:25,717 --> 00:02:26,586
may be true,

71
00:02:26,586 --> 00:02:28,685
but we have no source for it,

72
00:02:28,685 --> 00:02:30,350
so we do not tell it as

73
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:30,712
fact.

74
00:02:30,892 --> 00:02:33,693
Gandini's version is the one the page

75
00:02:33,693 --> 00:02:34,224
quotes.

76
00:02:34,573 --> 00:02:35,711
Why does this matter?

77
00:02:35,891 --> 00:02:38,993
Because retellings of the Countach story are

78
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:40,756
full of confident claims.

79
00:02:40,936 --> 00:02:43,030
A name that sounds like a story

80
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:43,908
attracts one.

81
00:02:44,088 --> 00:02:46,177
The honest version is short:

82
00:02:46,177 --> 00:02:49,087
the word is a Piedmontese expression of

83
00:02:49,087 --> 00:02:51,998
amazement, a worker's joke was adopted,

84
00:02:51,998 --> 00:02:54,982
it was coined around nineteen seventy or

85
00:02:54,982 --> 00:02:58,042
seventy-one, and that is what our sources

86
00:02:58,042 --> 00:02:58,937
can support.

87
00:02:59,287 --> 00:03:01,470
Why was the car built at all?

88
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:05,686
Wikipedia says Ferruccio Lamborghini wanted a successor

89
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:06,639
to the Miura,

90
00:03:06,639 --> 00:03:09,648
which by nineteen seventy had lost ground

91
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:12,436
to rivals such as the Ferrari Daytona.

92
00:03:12,616 --> 00:03:14,139
The chief engineer,

93
00:03:14,139 --> 00:03:17,986
Paolo Stanzani, started work in nineteen seventy

94
00:03:17,986 --> 00:03:20,391
under the project name L P one

95
00:03:20,391 --> 00:03:20,952
twelve.

96
00:03:21,132 --> 00:03:22,956
Test driver Bob Wallace,

97
00:03:22,956 --> 00:03:27,136
assistant engineer Massimo Parenti and Marcello Gandini

98
00:03:27,136 --> 00:03:29,340
of Bertone also worked on it.

99
00:03:29,689 --> 00:03:31,175
The first prototype,

100
00:03:31,175 --> 00:03:32,735
the L P five hundred,

101
00:03:32,735 --> 00:03:35,409
appeared at the Geneva Motor Show in

102
00:03:35,409 --> 00:03:36,969
nineteen seventy-one.

103
00:03:37,149 --> 00:03:40,057
The production L P four hundred followed

104
00:03:40,057 --> 00:03:41,874
in nineteen seventy-four.

105
00:03:42,054 --> 00:03:43,340
By our arithmetic,

106
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,270
that is three years between the prototype

107
00:03:46,270 --> 00:03:48,556
and the car customers could buy.

108
00:03:48,736 --> 00:03:52,151
The prototype's bodywork came from Bertone,

109
00:03:52,151 --> 00:03:54,533
and its chassis from Marchesi,

110
00:03:54,533 --> 00:03:57,710
which also built the production chassis.

111
00:03:58,060 --> 00:04:01,038
The Miura, which the Countach was meant

112
00:04:01,038 --> 00:04:03,253
to replace, is a car with its

113
00:04:03,253 --> 00:04:04,016
own story.

114
00:04:04,196 --> 00:04:07,819
Wikipedia says the engineers Giampaolo Dallara,

115
00:04:07,819 --> 00:04:10,901
Paolo Stanzani and Bob Wallace built the

116
00:04:10,901 --> 00:04:13,676
Miura prototype in their spare time,

117
00:04:13,676 --> 00:04:14,986
largely at night,

118
00:04:14,986 --> 00:04:16,758
in nineteen sixty-five.

119
00:04:16,938 --> 00:04:20,123
Ferruccio Lamborghini approved it after seeing the

120
00:04:20,123 --> 00:04:22,734
development car, and gave the engineers a

121
00:04:22,734 --> 00:04:23,370
free hand.

122
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:27,619
The Miura was the first high-performance production

123
00:04:27,619 --> 00:04:29,683
road car with a mid-engine,

124
00:04:29,683 --> 00:04:33,276
rear-wheel-drive layout, according to the page.

125
00:04:33,456 --> 00:04:34,792
Its three thousand,

126
00:04:34,792 --> 00:04:38,310
nine hundred twenty-nine cubic centimetre V twelve

127
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:40,491
sat sideways behind the driver.

128
00:04:40,671 --> 00:04:43,377
The Countach kept the mid-engine idea,

129
00:04:43,377 --> 00:04:45,443
but turned the engine around.

130
00:04:45,623 --> 00:04:47,361
We will come back to that in

131
00:04:47,361 --> 00:04:48,665
the comparison video.

132
00:04:49,015 --> 00:04:50,559
Now the second thing.

133
00:04:50,739 --> 00:04:53,293
The Countach prototype had a periscope.

134
00:04:53,473 --> 00:04:57,078
Wikipedia says that because rear visibility was

135
00:04:57,078 --> 00:05:00,530
poor, the prototype used a periscope supplied

136
00:05:00,530 --> 00:05:02,064
by Donnelly Mirrors.

137
00:05:02,244 --> 00:05:05,134
It had originally been developed for an

138
00:05:05,134 --> 00:05:06,172
E S V project,

139
00:05:06,172 --> 00:05:09,210
an experimental safety vehicle programme.

140
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:12,112
The production L P four hundred kept

141
00:05:12,112 --> 00:05:12,339
it.

142
00:05:12,519 --> 00:05:15,410
Later models used conventional mirrors.

143
00:05:15,759 --> 00:05:18,291
That is where the name Periscopio comes

144
00:05:18,291 --> 00:05:18,616
from.

145
00:05:18,796 --> 00:05:22,474
The RM Sotheby's catalogue calls the first-series

146
00:05:22,474 --> 00:05:25,252
cars the L P four hundred Periscopio,

147
00:05:25,252 --> 00:05:28,030
and says about one hundred fifty were

148
00:05:28,030 --> 00:05:31,183
built, according to the Countach Register.

149
00:05:31,363 --> 00:05:32,670
By our arithmetic,

150
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:35,573
that is about ninety-five percent of the

151
00:05:35,573 --> 00:05:38,477
one hundred fifty-seven L P four hundred

152
00:05:38,477 --> 00:05:40,001
cars Wikipedia lists.

153
00:05:40,181 --> 00:05:42,038
The two sources are close,

154
00:05:42,038 --> 00:05:43,037
not identical.

155
00:05:43,387 --> 00:05:46,580
The page also describes another trick for

156
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:47,358
reversing.

157
00:05:47,538 --> 00:05:49,682
Many drivers park by sitting on the

158
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:51,580
wide sill with the door raised,

159
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:54,091
and reversing while looking over the back

160
00:05:54,091 --> 00:05:55,561
of the car from outside.

161
00:05:55,741 --> 00:05:57,807
That is not a sales brochure.

162
00:05:57,987 --> 00:06:00,223
It is a practical workaround,

163
00:06:00,223 --> 00:06:03,383
and it appears in the encyclopaedia entry

164
00:06:03,383 --> 00:06:05,696
because owners actually do it.

165
00:06:06,046 --> 00:06:08,336
Rear visibility is the price of the

166
00:06:08,336 --> 00:06:08,728
shape.

167
00:06:08,908 --> 00:06:12,294
Wikipedia gives the dimensions of the production

168
00:06:12,294 --> 00:06:14,550
L P four hundred as four hundred

169
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:16,384
fourteen centimetres long,

170
00:06:16,384 --> 00:06:19,487
one hundred eighty-nine wide and one hundred

171
00:06:19,487 --> 00:06:20,263
seven tall.

172
00:06:20,443 --> 00:06:21,743
By our arithmetic,

173
00:06:21,743 --> 00:06:24,776
it is eighty-two centimetres wider than it

174
00:06:24,776 --> 00:06:25,354
is tall.

175
00:06:25,534 --> 00:06:27,662
With the engine behind the driver,

176
00:06:27,662 --> 00:06:29,352
a low, wide car with a high

177
00:06:29,352 --> 00:06:31,105
rear deck is hard to see out

178
00:06:31,105 --> 00:06:31,293
of.

179
00:06:31,642 --> 00:06:34,152
The scissor doors are the most famous

180
00:06:34,152 --> 00:06:35,780
feature of the Countach,

181
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:37,680
yet they did not start here.

182
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,261
Wikipedia says they first appeared on Marcello

183
00:06:41,261 --> 00:06:45,476
Gandini's nineteen sixty-eight Alfa Romeo Carabo concept.

184
00:06:45,656 --> 00:06:48,849
The doors hinge horizontally at the front,

185
00:06:48,849 --> 00:06:50,750
lift up and tilt forward,

186
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,575
supported by gas struts.

187
00:06:52,755 --> 00:06:54,805
The Countach made the idea famous,

188
00:06:54,805 --> 00:06:56,493
but it was not the first car

189
00:06:56,493 --> 00:06:57,156
to show it.

190
00:06:57,505 --> 00:06:59,142
There was a safety question.

191
00:06:59,322 --> 00:07:03,367
Wikipedia says engineers studied a removable kick-out

192
00:07:03,367 --> 00:07:07,029
windscreen and explosive bolts so that occupants

193
00:07:07,029 --> 00:07:09,319
could escape after a rollover.

194
00:07:09,499 --> 00:07:13,063
Neither idea was used on production cars.

195
00:07:13,243 --> 00:07:15,874
So the dramatic doors came without a

196
00:07:15,874 --> 00:07:18,067
documented emergency solution,

197
00:07:18,067 --> 00:07:20,332
a detail that is easy to forget

198
00:07:20,332 --> 00:07:22,159
when looking at a poster.

199
00:07:22,509 --> 00:07:26,375
Wikipedia also says the Countach prototype was

200
00:07:26,375 --> 00:07:28,140
destroyed on purpose.

201
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:31,054
The L P five hundred was crash-tested

202
00:07:31,054 --> 00:07:33,862
at MIRA in England on the twenty-first

203
00:07:33,862 --> 00:07:36,226
of March, nineteen seventy-four,

204
00:07:36,226 --> 00:07:38,665
to obtain European type approval.

205
00:07:38,845 --> 00:07:41,487
The show car that introduced the world

206
00:07:41,487 --> 00:07:42,599
to the Countach,

207
00:07:42,599 --> 00:07:43,642
in other words,

208
00:07:43,642 --> 00:07:44,894
was not preserved.

209
00:07:45,074 --> 00:07:46,594
It was used up so that the

210
00:07:46,594 --> 00:07:48,290
production car could be sold.

211
00:07:48,639 --> 00:07:52,174
The prototype was shown in nineteen seventy-one

212
00:07:52,174 --> 00:07:55,257
and crashed on the twenty-first of March,

213
00:07:55,257 --> 00:07:58,941
nineteen seventy-four, so by our arithmetic about

214
00:07:58,941 --> 00:08:01,573
three years passed between the two.

215
00:08:01,753 --> 00:08:04,209
The page does not give the exact

216
00:08:04,209 --> 00:08:05,514
date of the show,

217
00:08:05,514 --> 00:08:07,279
so this is approximate.

218
00:08:07,459 --> 00:08:08,636
The point stands:

219
00:08:08,636 --> 00:08:10,921
the car that made the name famous

220
00:08:10,921 --> 00:08:13,552
was destroyed in the process of making

221
00:08:13,552 --> 00:08:14,936
production possible.

222
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:16,406
Now the figures,

223
00:08:16,406 --> 00:08:18,154
from the Wikipedia table.

224
00:08:18,334 --> 00:08:20,198
The L P four hundred has a

225
00:08:20,198 --> 00:08:24,285
three thousand, nine hundred twenty-nine cubic centimetre

226
00:08:24,285 --> 00:08:27,440
V twelve rated at three hundred seventy-five

227
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:30,236
metric horsepower at eight thousand r p

228
00:08:30,236 --> 00:08:33,462
m, and three hundred sixty-one newton-metres.

229
00:08:33,642 --> 00:08:36,130
Dry weight is one thousand,

230
00:08:36,130 --> 00:08:38,065
sixty-five kilograms.

231
00:08:38,245 --> 00:08:40,519
Zero to a hundred in five point

232
00:08:40,519 --> 00:08:41,473
four seconds.

233
00:08:41,653 --> 00:08:44,033
One hundred fifty-seven were built.

234
00:08:44,382 --> 00:08:47,053
Top speed is where things get interesting.

235
00:08:47,233 --> 00:08:50,421
The table gives two hundred eighty-eight kilometres

236
00:08:50,421 --> 00:08:51,546
per hour measured,

237
00:08:51,546 --> 00:08:53,734
with three hundred fifteen claimed.

238
00:08:53,914 --> 00:08:55,224
By our arithmetic,

239
00:08:55,224 --> 00:08:57,769
the claim is nine percent above the

240
00:08:57,769 --> 00:09:01,333
measurement, or twenty-seven kilometres per hour.

241
00:09:01,513 --> 00:09:04,638
Wikipedia also lists a Walter Wolf special

242
00:09:04,638 --> 00:09:07,688
at three hundred fifteen or three hundred

243
00:09:07,688 --> 00:09:09,176
twenty-four claimed.

244
00:09:09,356 --> 00:09:12,177
Claims and measurements are different things.

245
00:09:12,526 --> 00:09:14,907
The L P four hundred S followed.

246
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:18,310
Wikipedia lists three hundred forty-nine or three

247
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:20,416
hundred fifty metric horsepower,

248
00:09:20,416 --> 00:09:22,981
depending on whether you read the table

249
00:09:22,981 --> 00:09:23,771
or the text,

250
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:26,863
with two hundred fifty-four kilometres per hour

251
00:09:26,863 --> 00:09:29,955
measured and two hundred seventy-nine point six

252
00:09:29,955 --> 00:09:30,481
claimed.

253
00:09:30,661 --> 00:09:33,214
Two hundred thirty-seven were built,

254
00:09:33,214 --> 00:09:34,987
in three series of fifty,

255
00:09:34,987 --> 00:09:37,256
one hundred five and eighty-two.

256
00:09:37,436 --> 00:09:39,190
It was slower than the car it

257
00:09:39,190 --> 00:09:39,735
replaced.

258
00:09:40,084 --> 00:09:43,402
Our arithmetic: fifty plus one hundred five

259
00:09:43,402 --> 00:09:46,797
plus eighty-two is two hundred thirty-seven,

260
00:09:46,797 --> 00:09:48,571
which matches the page.

261
00:09:48,751 --> 00:09:51,835
The S measured about thirty-four kilometres per

262
00:09:51,835 --> 00:09:53,738
hour slower than the L P four

263
00:09:53,738 --> 00:09:55,706
hundred, about twelve percent.

264
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:58,303
The page explains part of this:

265
00:09:58,303 --> 00:10:02,436
the optional rear wing improved high-speed stability,

266
00:10:02,436 --> 00:10:04,697
but cut top speed by at least

267
00:10:04,697 --> 00:10:06,880
sixteen kilometres per hour.

268
00:10:07,230 --> 00:10:08,531
Then the engine grew.

269
00:10:08,711 --> 00:10:10,575
The L P five hundred S has

270
00:10:10,575 --> 00:10:11,722
a four thousand,

271
00:10:11,722 --> 00:10:15,379
seven hundred fifty-four cubic centimetre V twelve,

272
00:10:15,379 --> 00:10:16,383
the page says,

273
00:10:16,383 --> 00:10:20,183
with three hundred seventy-five metric horsepower and

274
00:10:20,183 --> 00:10:23,409
two hundred ninety-three kilometres per hour.

275
00:10:23,589 --> 00:10:25,888
Three hundred twenty-one were built.

276
00:10:26,068 --> 00:10:29,810
The five thousand Quattrovalvole has five thousand,

277
00:10:29,810 --> 00:10:33,478
one hundred sixty-seven cubic centimetres and four

278
00:10:33,478 --> 00:10:36,193
hundred fifty-five metric horsepower,

279
00:10:36,193 --> 00:10:38,467
and six hundred ten were built.

